  "verbalization": "Nilutamide and Cyp2c19 are linked through a shared pathway involving androgen receptor antagonists. The evidence suggests that Nilutamide, as an androgen receptor antagonist, is included in the broader category of compounds that inhibit the androgen receptor, which in turn binds to Cyp2c19. This connection is reinforced by the fact that both Nilutamide and Flutamide, which are also androgen receptor antagonists, bind to Cyp2c19. The lowest common ancestor of Nilutamide and Flutamide is the (trifluoromethyl)benzenes, indicating a common structural feature that may contribute to their interaction with Cyp2c19. The scores from the paths suggest a strong, albeit slightly varying, relationship between Nilutamide and Cyp2c19, likely mediated through the androgen receptor pathway. The mechanism appears to involve the binding of these compounds to Cyp2c19, possibly through a shared structural motif or a common functional role in the metabolic pathway.",
